  "diagrams": {
    "hld": {
      "title": "High-Level Design",
      "mermaid": "flowchart TD\n  subgraph Bringup[\"Motor bring-up\"]\n    app_start[\"Start application<br/>firmware/app/app.c\"]\n    motor_if[\"Motor board contract<br/>firmware/interfaces/motor_board_if.h\"]\n    stm32_adapter[\"Configure STM32 motor board<br/>firmware/platforms/stm32/stm32_motor_board.c\"]\n    shield_driver[\"Initialize X-NUCLEO motor driver<br/>x_nucleo_ihm16m1_init\"]\n  end\n  subgraph MotorWiring[\"STSPIN830 motor wiring\"]\n    tim1[\"PWM timer<br/>TIM1#59; HAL_TIM_PWM_Start\"]\n    phase_pins[\"Three phase PWM pins<br/>PA8 / PA9 / PA10#59; GPIO_AF6_TIM1\"]\n    standby_pin[\"Standby output<br/>PC9#59; APP_MOTOR_STBY_GPIO_PIN\"]\n    fault_pin[\"Enable and fault input<br/>PB12#59; APP_MOTOR_EN_FAULT_GPIO_PIN\"]\n    motor_shield[\"STSPIN830 motor shield<br/>U / V / W phase interface\"]\n  end\n\n  app_start -->|motor_board_prepare| motor_if\n  motor_if -->|implementation| stm32_adapter\n  stm32_adapter -->|x_nucleo_ihm16m1_init| shield_driver\n  shield_driver -->|driver interface| motor_shield\n  stm32_adapter -->|HAL_TIM_PWM_Init and HAL_TIM_PWM_Start| tim1\n  tim1 -->|TIM_CHANNEL_1 / 2 / 3| phase_pins\n  phase_pins -->|U / V / W| motor_shield\n  stm32_adapter -->|HAL_GPIO_Init and HAL_GPIO_WritePin| standby_pin\n  standby_pin -->|STBY| motor_shield\n  motor_shield -->|EN_FAULT| fault_pin\n  fault_pin -->|HAL_GPIO_ReadPin| stm32_adapter",
      "authored_by_model": true,
      "node_notes": {
        "motor_shield": "This represents the physically wired STSPIN830 motor shield interface with U, V, W, standby, and enable-fault connections. The board facts and phase labels are documented in firmware/configs/app_config.h, while the driver API identifies the corresponding control signals.",
        "phase_pins": "PA8, PA9, and PA10 are configured together as high-speed GPIO alternate-function pins using GPIO_AF6_TIM1. These exact bindings come from APP_MOTOR_PHASE_U_GPIO_PIN, APP_MOTOR_PHASE_V_GPIO_PIN, APP_MOTOR_PHASE_W_GPIO_PIN, and configure_gpio.",
        "fault_pin": "PB12 is the enable and fault input with a pull-up configuration. The adapter reads it through HAL_GPIO_ReadPin when servicing the X_NUCLEO_IHM16M1_GPIO_EN_FAULT callback.",
        "tim1": "TIM1 generates the three PWM channels used for motor phase control. The platform adapter configures TIM1 and starts channels 1 through 3 with HAL_TIM_PWM_Init and HAL_TIM_PWM_Start in stm32_motor_board.c.",
        "stm32_adapter": "This STM32 platform adapter owns GPIO, TIM1, and callback wiring for the motor shield. configure_gpio, configure_timer, and motor_board_prepare in firmware/platforms/stm32/stm32_motor_board.c establish the HAL operations and driver initialization.",
        "shield_driver": "This software driver receives the STM32 callback table and selects the THREE_PWM_INPUTS mode while starting in standby. The x_nucleo_ihm16m1_init call and callback types are evidenced by firmware/drivers/x_nucleo_ihm16m1/src/x_nucleo_ihm16m1.c and its header.",
        "app_start": "This application entry point invokes motor_board_prepare and then reports the motor configuration. The evidence is firmware/app/app.c, where app_start calls the board contract and emits startup status logs.",
        "standby_pin": "PC9 is the STSPIN830 standby control and is configured as a push-pull output. The adapter drives it through HAL_GPIO_WritePin using APP_MOTOR_STBY_GPIO_PORT and APP_MOTOR_STBY_GPIO_PIN.",
        "motor_if": "This interface defines the motor_board_prepare contract used to keep application code independent of the STM32 implementation. Its declaration is in firmware/interfaces/motor_board_if.h and its implementation is supplied by stm32_motor_board.c."
      }
    },
    "lld": {
      "title": "Low-Level Design (Firmware Workflow)",
      "mermaid": "flowchart TD\n  subgraph AppBringup[\"Application bring-up path\"]\n    enter[\"Enter application<br/>firmware/app/app.c:8\"]\n    prepare[\"Configure GPIO, TIM1, and driver callbacks<br/>firmware/platforms/stm32/stm32_m…\"]\n    driver_init[\"Initialize three-PWM motor driver in standby<br/>firmware/platforms/stm32/stm32…\"]\n    status{\"motor_board_prepare succeeded — firmware/app/app.c:12\"}\n    success_log[\"Log successful STSPIN830 standby setup<br/>firmware/app/app.c:14\"]\n    failure_log[\"Log motor board preparation error<br/>firmware/app/app.c:16\"]\n    finish[\"Return from app_start<br/>firmware/app/app.c:18\"]\n  end\n\n  enter -->|motor_board_prepare| prepare\n  prepare -->|x_nucleo_ihm16m1_init| driver_init\n  driver_init -->|status| status\n  status -->|yes| success_log\n  status -->|no| failure_log\n  success_log -->  finish\n  failure_log -->  finish",
      "authored_by_model": true,
      "node_notes": {
